    "result_text": "The change is complete and the full test suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe spec required rejecting owner creation with **409 Conflict** when the new owner's lower-cased email is already used by another owner.\n\nI added a duplicate-email check in `addOwner` in `OwnerRestControllerV1.java`, placed right after the existing email validation/normalization step (where the DTO's email is already normalized to its trimmed, lower-cased form):\n\n```java\n// Reject the create when another owner already uses this email (compared case-insensitively\n// by lower-cased email). The DTO email is already normalized to its lower-cased form here.\nString normalizedEmail = ownerFieldsDto.getEmail();\nif (normalizedEmail != null) {\n    boolean emailInUse = this.clinicService.findAllOwners().stream()\n        .map(Owner::getEmail)\n        .filter(existing -> existing != null)\n        .map(existing -> existing.toLowerCase(Locale.ROOT))\n        .anyMatch(normalizedEmail::equals);\n    if (emailInUse) {\n        return new ResponseEntity<>(HttpStatus.CONFLICT);\n    }\n}\n```\n\nThis mirrors the existing telephone-uniqueness pattern in the same method. Absent/blank emails normalize to `null` and are skipped (uniqueness only applies when an email is present), and comparison is case-insensitive on both sides.\n\nThe new `AcceptanceTest.coreRejectsDuplicateEmail` test passes and `BUILD SUCCESS` \u2014 all tests green.",
